# Shell scripts are LF, always. install.sh is served from
# raw.githubusercontent straight into `sh`, and a CRLF shebang makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter whose name ends in a carriage return --
# "/bin/sh^M", which does not exist, for an error that names a path that
# looks perfectly correct.
#
# Scoped to *.sh on purpose. A repository-wide rule here would renormalize a
# working tree that is CRLF throughout.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Signed release bytes. Tests verify a published Ed25519 signature over this exact
# file, so its line endings must never be converted on checkout.
crates/registry/tests/fixtures/argocd-manifest.json -text
crates/registry/tests/fixtures/argocd-0.3.0-manifest.json -text
crates/registry/tests/fixtures/flux-0.4.0-manifest.json -text

# Package fixtures (#562): every file is named by its SHA-256 in its package's digest list,
# and the signed one's list carries a signature, so no byte may change on checkout.
crates/registry/tests/fixtures/packages/** -text
crates/registry/tests/fixtures/trust/example-release.json -text

# Go source is LF, as gofmt writes it. The generator's output is compared with
# the committed file byte for byte, and gofmt -l lists a CRLF file as
# unformatted.
*.go text eol=lf
